   "blob": "8724bfbef6638e8efa371e78a7c026c28ca2dc62",
   "readme3": "**Design-only as of 2026-10-18 (19ca8d4): the two program documents are the only artifacts; P2–P4 plan adapter code and live runs.** MechanicalWorkflows is a family of composable workflow libraries and applications, not a workflow engine/scheduler, Beads status store, Forge verifier or new CAC runtime (it does ship an optional Furnace executor host adapter: apps/development-rig/src/furnace-process-executor.ts and furnace-app.ts, witnessed 2026-10-15).",
   "readme17": "- Agent SDK or Pi designs may execute a step but do not retroactively establish source evidence (one bounded Claude Agent SDK step witnessed 2026-10-15 under CLI opt-in; no Pi adapter is wired at 19ca8d4).",
   "readme21": "As of 2026-10-18 (19ca8d4) these are interface/theorem research requirements, not a claim that source code was modified or native workflows were run.",
   "contractsPath": "docs/programs/cac-workflow-composition-2026-10-18/01-composition-contracts.md",
   "contractsBlob": "5e6c16c0c0415f1df837671a949ee9f2c6a5fed2",
   "contracts4": "Under the proposed contract a workflow step would expose its typed input/output, effect scope, authority/version requirements, idempotency/retry behavior, verifier predicate and native evidence reference. No current MechanicalWorkflows step type exposes effect scope, authority/version or idempotency/retry fields; docs/11 D-01 adds a primitive only when a real consumer demonstrates it. A composition validates (a) type compatibility, (b) local postcondition establishing successor precondition, (c) independent permissions for each effect, validated by the host/native admission owner, not by MechanicalWorkflows, (d) checkpoint/retry semantics checked against the producer's native contract where one exists (Furnace 0.1.0 ships run resume / work retry but no effect-idempotency contract), and (e) an explicit bridge invariant/certificate (CAC 0.1 Bridge rule) from local validations to the overall intended claim; no bridge checker exists at HEAD.",
   "contracts6": "Use \\`CACWorkflowCompositionV0\\` as a concept only. It can point to existing workflow step and source artifact IDs, but it must not create new authoritative IDs for Beads tasks, Forge operations/gates, Furnace attempts, Git revisions or HyperUnix answers (a non-exhaustive list).",
   "documents": [
    "docs/programs/cac-workflow-composition-2026-10-18/01-composition-contracts.md",
    "docs/programs/cac-workflow-composition-2026-10-18/README.md"
   ],
   "measuredBy": "ws-03 (g10-work-s59), read-only git show/ls-tree of the local checkout",
   "measuredUtc": "2026-10-23T21:47:35Z"
  }
 },
